<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fall of Nineveh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">612 BCE</span> · Also known as destroyed Nineveh · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medo-babylonian-conquest-of-the-assyrian-empire">Medo-Babylonian conquest of the Assyrian Empire</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> was the destruction of the Assyrian capital in 612 BCE by a coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a>. It was the decisive blow to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and a founding moment of Median power. The event also appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> profile as part of the long history of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fall-of-nineveh.jpg" alt="Fall of Nineveh" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (Mu-tamajo) むーたんじょ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fall_of_nineveh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
